+
+# Merge patch rejects non-JSON input and shares helpers via json.ts
+
+## Context
+RFC 7386 defines the merge on JSON values. Following dl-003, non-JSON input (undefined, NaN, Date,
+cycles) should not be silently accepted. The check and member-setting helpers lived in `patch.ts`.
+
+## Decision
+`applyMergePatch` throws if `target` or `patch` is not a JSON value. Non-object patches replace the
+target (cloned); a non-object target is treated as `{}`; `null` members delete. Results are fresh
+values and `__proto__` is an ordinary member. Shared helpers moved to `src/json.ts`.
+
+## Consequences
+Inputs are never mutated. Arrays are replaced wholesale, as the RFC requires; a `null` inside an
+array is kept, and a null patch yields `null`.
